@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`
IMPORT `nii-statuses-chapters`
IMPORT `nii-s238-housewife`
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s335-branches`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-33 feeds row IL-08's s 335: the statuses s 335 reads, DERIVED from the facts of the person on a day.
-- `nii-il08-nouns.l4` and `nii-s335-branches.l4` are row IL-08's modules, vendored here UNCHANGED (their
-- sha256 are in VENDORED.sha256) because imports resolve only beside the importing file.
--
-- The record `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` that IL-08 declares has thirteen fields. The
-- capstone fills them by hand; this module fills them from `A person for the statuses of the Law`, with a
-- woman's marriage, her spouse, her widowhood and the fact of a widow's pension where s 238 needs them.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The statuses s 335 reads, from facts`

@ref NII s 335(a)-(i); ss 2A, 75, 150, 158, 180-181, 195, 223, 238, 240, 6B
GIVEN p     IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      m     IS A `A woman's marriage`
      sp    IS A MAYBE `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      wd    IS A MAYBE `A widowing`
      pf    IS A `A widow's pension fact`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd    IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A `A person in a contribution period, for section 335`
`s 335 — the statuses of` p `, her marriage` m `, her spouse` sp `, her widowhood` wd `, her widow's pension` pf `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
    `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` WITH
        `the calendar year of the period`                                            IS DATE_YEAR `the day`
        `an employee or a self-employed person`                                      IS (p's work)'s `an employee` OR (p's work)'s `a self-employed person`
        `an Israeli resident`                                                        IS `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`)
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                   IS `s 240 — insured under Chapter 11:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                      IS `s 238 — a housewife:` p `, her marriage` m `, her spouse` sp `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                                IS
            CONSIDER wd
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST w THEN `s 238 — a widow pensioner:` p `, widowed` w `, her pension` pf `, reading` rd
        `insured under Chapter 5`                                                    IS `s 75 — insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `insured under Chapter 6`                                                    IS `s 150 — insured under Chapter 6:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158`   IS `s 158 — insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                        IS `s 6B — Chapters 7 and 8 do not apply to the person:` p
        `an employee insured under Chapter 8`                                        IS `s 180-181 — a worker insured under Chapter 8:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `insured under Chapter 9`                                                    IS `s 195 — insured under Chapter 9:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
        `insured for long-term care`                                                 IS `s 223 — insured for long-term care:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd

@ref NII s 335, lines 3610-3620; row IL-08's rule
GIVEN p     IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      m     IS A `A woman's marriage`
      sp    IS A MAYBE `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      wd    IS A MAYBE `A widowing`
      pf    IS A `A widow's pension fact`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd    IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` p `, her marriage` m `, her spouse` sp `, her widowhood` wd `, her widow's pension` pf `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
    `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for`
        (`s 335 — the statuses of` p `, her marriage` m `, her spouse` sp `, her widowhood` wd `, her widow's pension` pf `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd)
